-- GRADED under `build-run`. The correct answer is 6, derived by hand: `A.shrink` is
-- alias-qualified to amod1684's own standalone, whose body is `n + 1`, applied to 5.
-- `medaka run` agrees and prints 6. The BUILT BINARY prints a list instead -- the call
-- was routed to the prelude `Arbitrary.shrink`. Both at exit 0, no diagnostic on any
-- channel: run and the binary disagree with each other. See claim.txt.
import amod1684 as A

main = println (A.shrink 5)
